:: Title_Screen [title] {"position":"300,100","size":"100,100"}
# The Timeless Office
*Humorous Time-Travel Comedy* • *Lighthearted, self-aware, irreverent, slapstick with romantic and adult-tinged absurdity*

> [!NOTE]
> **Content Advisory:** Mature 18+ (Explicit Uncensored Content)

**The Conflict:** Jordan must collect scattered artifact pieces across three timelines, solve era-specific puzzles amid reincarnated coworkers in hilarious situations, and complete the ritual before the timelines fully merge and collapse, all triggered by his accidental activation during a romantic dare.

**Themes:** Corporate Absurdity Across Eras, Accidental Timeline Chaos, Reincarnation and Recurring Romances, Self-Aware Cult Satire, The Comedy of Existential Stakes

**Protagonist:** Jordan Hale, an impulsive and easily-dared new real estate agent whose flaw is leaping into romantic or reckless situations without thinking. His world role is the fresh hire at a quirky firm who accidentally becomes the catalyst for an ancient cult ritual. His moral wound is a light, comedic aversion to responsibility that he masks with jokes and flirtation rather than any deep trauma.

**Antagonist:** Victor Kane (modern-day coworker and self-appointed cult expert), who appears as the king's advisor in the medieval era and the dorm disciplinarian in the 1960s. His motivation is to treat the timeline crisis as a universe-ending catastrophe that only he can avert. Opposing worldview: deadly seriousness about the ritual versus the story's overall joke tone. Leverage: insider knowledge of the artifacts and reincarnations that he dispenses in over-the-top, comedic monologues.

### Emergent Character Traits
* **<span style='color:#FF6B35'>Impulsiveness</span>**: The drive to act on dares, flirtations, and sudden opportunities without weighing consequences, frequently triggering timeline shifts and chaotic but surprisingly effective solutions.
* **<span style='color:#4ECDC4'>Caution</span>**: Methodical assessment of timeline risks and careful puzzle-solving to prevent total collapse, serving as the counterbalance to reckless choices.

