:: Dramatis_Personae [codex] {"position":"260,240","size":"100,100"}
## 👥 Dramatis Personae (Cast of Characters)

### Jordan Hale *(protagonist)*
Fresh out of a string of dead-end jobs, Jordan joined the quirky real estate firm on a whim after losing a bet. During a reckless office dare with a coworker, he accidentally activated the ancient time-shifting artifact hidden in the CEO's office, triggering the timeline collapse.

### Victor Kane *(antagonist)*
A mid-level coworker and self-proclaimed occult hobbyist who has studied the firm's hidden cult artifacts for years, Victor sees himself as the only one qualified to prevent universal collapse.

### Sophia Reed *(ally)*
Jordan's quick-witted coworker and initial date partner, Sophia has quietly suspected the office's reincarnation cycle for months through recurring dreams of past lives as a courtier and co-ed.

### Elena Voss *(ally)*
The firm's meticulous HR coordinator and part-time cult researcher, Elena has spent years documenting the building's era shifts in secret spreadsheets.

### Finn Harper *(ally)*
The firm's slacker IT guy and resident stoner, Finn has been casually high during every previous minor time hiccup and treats the full crisis like an extended lunch break.

### Reginald Thorne *(neutral)*
The eccentric CEO whose bloodline is tied to the original cult ritual, Reginald cycles between modern executive, medieval king, and 1960s dorm warden without ever fully realizing the pattern.

### Clara Bennett *(neutral)*
The sharp-tongued receptionist who has witnessed three minor time bleeds and keeps a secret stash of era-specific artifacts in her desk drawer for 'emergencies.'

### Brenda Slate *(antagonist_ally)*
Victor's ambitious junior associate who handles the firm's 'special projects' and has been groomed as his ritual second-in-command.

### Melanie Voss *(Jordan's initial romantic coworker and recurring consort)*
### Ron the Broker *(Comic relief male colleague and timeline skeptic)*
### Victor Kane *(Modern cult expert and antagonist delivering doom monologues)*
### Isolde the Enchantress *(Reincarnated harem member and seductive guide)*
### Dorm Mother Ethel *(Reincarnated authority figure enforcing rules with hidden romantic streaks)*
### Warden Victor *(Victor's reincarnated disciplinarian form)*
### The Artifact Spirit *(Mysterious narrator and puzzle hint giver)*

